From f9859b80a39c5a133612363538f8a343d7f4a447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Stackhouse <joseph.stackhouse@stack-tech.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:01:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bridge no-P2P CUDA boundaries through mapped pinned staging

These cards expose no peer-to-peer path, so every cross-card boundary stages
through host memory over a Gen1 x1 link. This makes that staging explicit:
scheduler-visible CUDA ownership plus a fixed four-slot mapped pinned bridge
for boundaries up to 64 MiB, with event-ordered slot reuse so a slot is never
rewritten while a consumer is still reading it.

Lossless by construction: it changes where bytes are staged, not what they
contain. Deterministic output is retained.

Default-off, selected by GGML_CUDA_MAPPED_HOST_BRIDGE=1.
---
